### Phase 4: Database Security — Enable RLS on Unprotected Tables

| Table | Action |
|---|---|
| `user_2fa_factors` | Enable RLS + policy: users can only access their own rows |
| `user_2fa_challenges` | Enable RLS + policy: users can only access their own rows |
| `user_2fa_attempts` | Enable RLS + policy: users can only access their own rows |
| `budget_categories` | Enable RLS + policy: authenticated read, admin/accountant write |
| `expense_budget_mapping` | Enable RLS + policy: admin/accountant full access |
| `expense_financial_mapping` | Enable RLS + policy: admin/accountant full access |

---

### Phase 5: Database Security — Harden Functions

Set `search_path = public` on all 48 public functions to prevent search_path hijacking. Functions with `SECURITY DEFINER` (8 functions including `current_user_role`, `current_user_employee_id`, `get_managed_employee_ids`, etc.) are especially critical.

---

### Phase 6: Database Security — Fix Overly Permissive Policies

| Table | Policy | Issue | Fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| `audit_logs` | `System can insert audit logs` | `WITH CHECK (true)` | Restrict to `service_role` or `authenticated` |
| `budget_allocations` | `budget_allocations_policy` | `USING (true)` — all access open | Restrict to admin/accountant roles |

---

### Phase 7: Database Security — Review SECURITY DEFINER Views

The 4 views (`monthly_attendance_summary`, `payroll_allowances_summary`, `expense_financial_mapping_view`, `employee_balance_summary`) are set with `SECURITY DEFINER`. These will be changed to `SECURITY INVOKER` so that RLS on underlying tables is respected.

---

